    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dymas</span></b> , antis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δύμας</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the father of
			Hecuba</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 11, 761</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 7, 320</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">111</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dy-mantis</span></b> , ĭdis,
				adj., <i>of Dymas</i>: proles, i. e.
				<i>Hecuba;</i> and, as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dyman-tis</span></b> , ĭdis,
				f., <i>the daughter of Dymas</i>, i. e.
				<i>Hecuba</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				620</span></i>.</div>
